    "primaryWitnesses": [
      {
        "ref": "Acts 25:13",
        "textualBasisJa": "Now when some days had passed, King Agrippa and Bernice arrived at Caesarea and greeted Festus."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 25:22",
        "textualBasisJa": "Agrippa said to Festus, “I also would like to hear the man myself.” “Tomorrow,” he said, “you shall hear him.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 25:23",
        "textualBasisJa": "So on the next day, when Agrippa and Bernice had come with great pomp, and they had entered into the place of hearing with the commanding officers and the principal men of the city, at the command of Festus, Paul was brought in."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 25:24",
        "textualBasisJa": "Festus said, “King Agrippa, and all men who are here present with us, you see this man about whom all the multitude of the Jews petitioned me, both at Jerusalem and here, crying that he ought not to live any longer."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 25:26",
        "textualBasisJa": "of whom I have no certain thing to write to my lord. Therefore I have brought him out before you, and especially before you, King Agrippa, that, after examination I may have something to write."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 26:1",
        "textualBasisJa": "Agrippa said to Paul, “You may speak for yourself.” Then Paul stretched out his hand, and made his defense."
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 26:2",
        "textualBasisJa": "“I think myself happy, King Agrippa, that I am to make my defense before you today concerning all the things the Jews accuse me of,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 26:7",
        "textualBasisJa": "which our twelve tribes, earnestly serving night and day, hope to attain. Concerning this hope I am accused by the Jews, King Agrippa!"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 26:19",
        "textualBasisJa": "“Therefore, King Agrippa, I was not disobedient to the heavenly vision,"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 26:27",
        "textualBasisJa": "King Agrippa, do you believe the prophets? I know that you believe.”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 26:28",
        "textualBasisJa": "Agrippa said to Paul, “With a little persuasion are you trying to make me a Christian?”"
      },
      {
        "ref": "Acts 26:32",
        "textualBasisJa": "Agrippa said to Festus, “This man might have been set free if he had not appealed to Caesar.”"
      }
    ],
